{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(values):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers using the heap sort algorithm.\n    This implementation avoids using Python's built-in `heapq` module to demonstrate the algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(values)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Build a max-heap\n    # The last parent node is at index (n // 2) - 1 for 0-indexed array\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _sift_down(arr, i, n - 1)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        # Move current root to end\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]\n        # Call max heapify on the reduced heap\n        _sift_down(arr, 0, i - 1)\n    return arr\n\ndef _sift_down(arr, start, end):\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to maintain the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at 'start'.\n    'end' is the index of the last element in the heap.\n    \"\"\"\n    root = start\n    while True:\n        child = 2 * root + 1\n        if child > end:\n            break\n\n        # Find the largest child\n        swap = root\n        if arr[swap] < arr[child]:\n            swap = child\n        if child + 1 <= end and arr[swap] < arr[child + 1]:\n            swap = child + 1\n\n        if swap == root:\n            break\n        arr[root], arr[swap] = arr[swap], arr[root]\n        root = swap"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\n\ndef wind_chill(velocity_kmh: float, temperature_c: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index using the Canadian apparent temperature formula,\n    rounded to the nearest integer with half-up semantics.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate v^0.16\n    v_pow_0_16 = math.pow(velocity_kmh, 0.16)\n\n    # Apply the Canadian apparent temperature formula\n    # apparent_temp = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*v^0.16 + 0.3965*T*v^0.16\n    raw_wind_chill = (\n        13.12\n        + 0.6215 * temperature_c\n        - 11.37 * v_pow_0_16\n        + 0.3965 * temperature_c * v_pow_0_16\n    )\n\n    # Round to the nearest integer with half-up semantics\n    if raw_wind_chill >= 0:\n        rounded_value = int(math.floor(raw_wind_chill + 0.5))\n    else:\n        rounded_value = int(math.ceil(raw_wind_chill - 0.5))\n\n    return rounded_value"}
