{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix: List[List[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the path from the top-left to the bottom-right cell in a square matrix\n    with the maximum average cost, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n    \n    # dp[r][c] will store the maximum sum to reach cell (r, c)\n    dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Initialize the top-left cell\n    dp[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row: cells can only be reached from the left\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c-1] + float(matrix[0][c])\n\n    # Fill the first column: cells can only be reached from above\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r-1][0] + float(matrix[r][0])\n\n    # Fill the rest of the DP table\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            # The maximum sum to reach (r, c) is the current cell's value\n            # plus the maximum sum from either the cell directly above (r-1, c)\n            # or the cell directly to the left (r, c-1).\n            dp[r][c] = max(dp[r-1][c], dp[r][c-1]) + float(matrix[r][c])\n\n    # The maximum total cost to reach the bottom-right cell (n-1, n-1)\n    max_total_cost = dp[n-1][n-1]\n    \n    # The number of cells visited in any path from top-left to bottom-right\n    # in an N*N matrix, moving only right or down, is always (2*N - 1).\n    num_cells_in_path = (2 * n - 1)\n    \n    # Calculate the maximum average\n    max_average = max_total_cost / num_cells_in_path\n    \n    return max_average"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Union\n\ndef multiply_elements(input_tuple: Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]) -> Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Multiplies adjacent elements of a tuple of numbers.\n    The i-th element of the output tuple is the product of input_tuple[i] and input_tuple[i+1].\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(input_tuple[i] * input_tuple[i+1] for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1))"}
