{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "def max_sum_list(lists: list[list[float]]) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the sublist in a list of lists whose sum of elements is the highest.\n    If multiple sublists have the same highest sum, the first one encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lists:\n        return []\n\n    max_found_list = lists[0]\n    max_current_sum = sum(lists[0])\n\n    for current_list in lists[1:]:\n        current_sum = sum(current_list)\n        if current_sum > max_current_sum:\n            max_current_sum = current_sum\n            max_found_list = current_list\n\n    return max_found_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is strictly smaller than its\n    corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(b) > len(a):\n        # If the second tuple is longer, not all its elements can have a\n        # corresponding element in the first tuple to be smaller than.\n        return False\n\n    for x, y in zip(a, b):\n        if not (y < x):\n            return False\n    return True"}
